st, `rich/markup.py` seems like the most relevant file.\n\nLet's start by creating a reproduction script to confirm the issue.\nIf it's about escaping trailing backslashes in markup, I should try something like `rich.markup.escape(\"text\\\\\")`.\n\nWait, the issue is \"escaping trailing backslash\". In many markup languages, a backslash is used to escape the next character. If a backslash is at the end of the string, it might be handled incorrectly.\n\nLet's try to reproduce it.", "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 4311, "completion_tokens": 223, "cached_tokens": 0, "total_tokens": 4534}, "model": "/kaggle/input/models/google/gemma-4/other/gemma-4-31b-it-qat-w4a16-ct/2"}, {"timestamp": 1794032002.0057752, "elapsed_s": 31.466, "type": "tool_call", "author": "swe_baseline_agent", "tool": "run_command", "args": {"command": "cat > /tmp/repro.py <<'EOF'\nfrom rich.markup import escape\nprint(f\"'{escape('text\\\\')}'\")\nEOF\npython3 /tmp/repro.py\n"}, "model": "/kaggle/input/models/google/gemma-4/other/gemma-4-31b-it-qat-w4a16-ct/2"}, {"timestamp": 1794032002.1544626, "elapsed_s": 31.614, "type": "tool_response", "author": "swe_baseline_agent", "tool": "run_command", "result": "{\"status\": \"ok\", \"stdout\": \"'text\\\\'\\n\", \"stderr\": \"Error in sitecustomize; set PYTHONVERBOSE for traceback:\\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'wrapt'\\n\", \"exit_code\": 0}"}, {"timestamp": 1794032006.3886218, "elapsed_s": 35.849, "type": "thinking", "author": "swe_baseline_agent", "content": "The output is `'text\\'`. Wait, `escape('text\\\\')` resulted in `'text\\'`.\nWait, in Python, `'text\\\\'` is a string with a single backslash at the end.\nThe output `'text\\'` is also a string with a single backslash at the end (the outer quotes are from my print statement).\n\nLet's check what `escape` is supposed to do.\nUsually, `escape` should escape characters that have special meaning in markup.\nIn `rich`, markup uses `[` and `]`.\n\nLet's see `rich/markup.py`.", "usage": {"prompt_to